.TH GSR-UI 1 "2024-08-01" "sgsr-ui" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sgsr-ui \- A fullscreen overlay UI for GPU Screen Recorder in the style of ShadowPlay
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgsr-ui\fP is a fullscreen overlay UI for GPU Screen Recorder in the style of ShadowPlay.
The application is currently primarily designed for X11 but it can run on Wayland as well through XWayland, with some caveats because of Wayland limitations.
.PP
This interface is built mainly for use with keyboard shortcuts.
When launched for the first time, it runs in the background, ready to receive shortcut keys.
On a subsequent launch, the fullscreen overlay UI appears.
.SH SYSTEM TRAY
SourisGSR registers an \fBorg.kde.StatusNotifierItem\fP tray icon (toggle it
with "Show system tray icon" in global settings, takes effect on restart).
Left/middle click shows or hides the overlay. There is no right-click menu in
this version; use hotkeys, the overlay buttons or \fBgsr-ui-cli\fP(1) instead.
The tray lives in \fBgsr-ui\fP only and never in embedding SDKs.
.SH AUDIO VOLUMES
Audio volume is set \fBper audio input\fP: every input row in the Audio
settings has its own 0-100 slider (drag, arrow keys, mouse wheel,
double-click resets to 100), stored as a \fB|vol=NN|\fP suffix on that input.
All volumes are recording-only and never touch the system mixer. There are no
global volume controls in the UI; the engine keeps
\fB-mic-volume\fP/\fB-system-volume\fP/\fB-app-volume\fP as deprecated
CLI/SDK fallbacks (see \fBgpu-screen-recorder\fP(1)).
